# tools/ is ALLOW-BY-DEFAULT. Each tool owns its own .gitignore for its build output
# (node_modules/, dist/, temp files), which is where that knowledge belongs and where
# it keeps working if the tool is ever moved or extracted.
#
# This replaced a `tools/*` blanket plus a `!tools/appstore-screenshots/` negation.
# That worked, but made every NEW tool invisible until someone remembered to add
# another negation, and nothing warns you: an untracked-but-ignored directory never
# shows up in `git status`. If you add a tool, give it a .gitignore, not a rule here.
#
# (For the record, since the old form looked like a typo: the blanket had to be
# `tools/*` and not `tools/`, because git does not descend into an excluded directory,
# so a negation under a plain `tools/` can never be evaluated.)

nul
